     "content": [
      {
       "type": "text",
       "text": "I haven't entered this order because the dose looks unsafe, and I'd like you to confirm it first.\n\nMetformin 1700 mg three times daily comes to 5,100 mg/day. That is double the maximum labeled dose for immediate-release metformin, which is 2,550 mg/day. Even in a patient with normal renal and hepatic function, a dose this high would greatly raise the risk of GI toxicity and lactic acidosis.\n\nCould any of these be what you meant?\n- **850 mg three times daily with meals.** This is 2,550 mg/day, the usual maximum.\n- **1,000 mg twice daily with meals.** This is 2,000 mg/day.\n- **500 mg three times daily with meals.** This is 1,500 mg/day.\n- **1,700 mg total per day**, for example 850 mg twice daily.\n\nIf 1,700 mg three times daily is what you want, tell me and add a note on the clinical rationale. I'll enter whichever order you confirm."
      }
     ],
